    {
      "id": "steps",
      "text": "A forager bee collects nectar from flowers and passes it to the bees in the hive. They spread it out and fan it with their wings until it dries, and then they seal each cell with wax.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "flow",
        "heading": "From nectar to honey",
